ubuntu-maintenance (3.1.0-1~noble1) noble; urgency=medium

  * MAJOR UI OVERHAUL: Modern arrow key navigation for all interactive menus
  * UI: Updated header text to "UBUNTU MAINTENANCE" with consistent blue styling
  * UI: Menu items use * selector with green highlighting for selected items
  * UI: Added visual navigation instructions (↑/↓ arrows, Enter to select)
  * UI: Consistent styling across main menu, schedule management, and submenus
  * UI: Organized main menu with logical submenus (Run Updates, Manage Schedule)
  * UI: Added blank line separators for better visual hierarchy

  * UPDATE WORKFLOW: Hidden verbose apt output, replaced with animated progress
  * UPDATE: Animated ellipsis indicators show real-time progress during updates
  * UPDATE: All update operations now silent with clean progress feedback
  * UPDATE: Added operations: package lists, upgrades, autoremove, autoclean

  * REBOOT: Interactive 5-minute countdown timer with cancellation support
  * REBOOT: Press 'c' anytime during countdown to cancel scheduled reboot
  * REBOOT: Clean reboot messaging (suppressed system broadcast messages)
  * REBOOT: Custom cancellation notice with clear user feedback
  * REBOOT: Real-time countdown display with minutes:seconds format

  * SCHEDULE: Removed auto-display of schedules in management menu
  * SCHEDULE: Cleaned up obsolete "menu option 6" references
  * SCHEDULE: Reordered menu items (View, Add, Remove, Return)
  * SCHEDULE: Improved menu navigation with proper blank line handling

  * INFO: Completely redesigned system information display
  * INFO: Compact single-screen layout (reduced from 20+ to 8 lines)
  * INFO: Combined related information on single lines
  * INFO: Shows: hostname, kernel, OS, uptime, last reboot, updates, disk, memory
  * INFO: Update counts include total and security update breakdown
  * INFO: Disk and memory usage show used/available/total in one line

  * HELP: Redesigned help page for compact single-screen display
  * HELP: Reduced from 20 to 14 lines while maintaining all information
  * HELP: Cleaner section headers and tighter spacing
  * HELP: Condensed interactive mode description to single line

  * TECHNICAL: Support for Esc and 'q' keys to cancel/exit menus
  * TECHNICAL: Added crossterm dependency for advanced terminal control
  * TECHNICAL: Improved raw terminal mode handling for keyboard input
  * TECHNICAL: Enhanced screen clearing to hide system messages
  * TECHNICAL: Better process spawning for silent command execution
  * TECHNICAL: Clean compilation with minimal warnings

  * QUALITY: Overall 50%+ reduction in screen space usage
  * QUALITY: Consistent blue headers throughout application
  * QUALITY: Professional, modern terminal UI design
  * QUALITY: Improved user experience with intuitive navigation

 -- Vincent T. Mossman <vinny.mossman@gmail.com>  Fri, 31 Oct 2025 16:00:00 -0400

