ubuntu-maintenance (3.0.0-1~noble1) noble; urgency=medium

  * MAJOR UPDATE: Complete Rust rewrite
  * Compile-time memory safety guarantees (no buffer overflows, use-after-free)
  * Zero runtime memory leaks guaranteed by Rust's ownership system
  * Modern error handling with Result and Option types
  * Binary renamed from system_update to ubuntu-maintenance
  * Log file renamed to /var/log/ubuntu_maintenance.log
  * Colored terminal output for better visibility
  * Modern CLI parsing with clap library
  * All functionality from v2.1.0 maintained
  * Enhanced security through Rust's type system
  * ~1.4MB single binary with no runtime dependencies
  * Improved code maintainability and reliability

