ubuntu-maintenance (2.0.0-1) jammy; urgency=medium

  * Initial PPA release (version 2.0.0)
  * Complete rewrite with production-ready security hardening
  * Fixed all memory leaks (6 allocations without free())
  * Replaced unsafe strcpy() with bounds-checked alternatives
  * Added comprehensive buffer overflow protection
  * Implemented input validation on all user input
  * Added comprehensive error handling throughout
  * Created proper header file structure
  * Replaced inefficient 200+ line function with sprintf()
  * Fixed missing return value in main()
  * Implemented complete system information page
  * Added dry-run mode for safe preview of changes
  * Comprehensive logging to /var/log/system_update.log
  * Safe reboot with 5-minute delay instead of immediate
  * Added cancellable shutdown with user notification
  * Implemented long and short command-line options
  * Added complete help system with usage examples
  * Sudo privilege checking for security
  * Better output formatting and user feedback
  * Progress indicators for long-running operations
  * Exit codes for scripting integration
  * Command execution logging with exit codes
  * Fallback logging when primary log unavailable
  * Interactive menu with proper input validation
  * Added apt autoclean to all update modes
  * Comprehensive documentation and man pages

